  "body": "### Steps To Reproduce\n\n1. Create a component with a group, and inside the group a nested component (if the nested is directly under the component root the bug does not occur).\n2. Create a copy.\n3. In the copy, swap the nested component to another one.\n4. Then do a \"reset overrides\" in the nested component.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe nested component should become the same as is in the main component (effectively undoing the swap).\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nAn error page appears.\n\nIn production, the error trace shows a referential integrity error, with a missing swap slot. In the development environment we see an assertion failing with `invalid-shape-id`.\n\n### Technical info\n\nThere was an error getting the shape in the main component. In development, an assert detected the missing shape id. In production, where asserts are disabled, the id passed but caused that the operation to undo the swap is not executed. So the shape ended in a status that it is still swapped but it does not have a slot. This is what is detected by the validator.",
